      "created_at": "2025-09-28T03:06:11Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-09-28T03:06:11Z",
      "body": "You can adjust these using the custom CSS feature (Settings > Custom CSS). For your specific set up, I think this should be a good starting point:\n\n```\n/* Give proportional sizes to columns in the download client widget */ \ntable.downloads-widget-table {\n  # Job name\n  --header-name-size: 70 !important;\n  --col-name-size: 70 !important;\n\n  # Progress\n  --header-progress-size: 30 !important;\n  --col-progress-size: 30 !important;\n\n  # File size\n  --header-size-size: 10 !important;\n  --col-size-size: 10 !important;\n\n  # Finish time\n  --header-time-size: 20 !important;\n  --col-time-size: 20 !important;\n}\n```\n\nbut you can adjust the numbers. A higher number will make that section larger (these values are relative to each other). Note that `--header-*` adjusts the size of  the header row, while `--col-*` adjusts the size of the rest of the rows.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
