      "body": "Oops, the `# Column name` is messing up the line immediately after (mixed my programming languages up), so the header CSS isn't applying.\n\n```\n/* Give proportional sizes to columns in the download client widget */ \ntable.downloads-widget-table {\n  /* File name */\n  --header-name-size: 70 !important;\n  --col-name-size: 70 !important;\n\n  /* Progress */\n  --header-progress-size: 30 !important;\n  --col-progress-size: 30 !important;\n\n  /* File size */\n  --header-size-size: 10 !important;\n  --col-size-size: 10 !important;\n\n  /* Finish time */\n  --header-time-size: 20 !important;\n  --col-time-size: 20 !important;\n}\n``` \n\nThat should do it. You can also remove the [comments](https://www.w3schools.com/css/css_comments.asp) completely, since they're just there as notes.",
